# Quiz auto-scoring and partial marks

Canonical formula (`QuizPartialCredit.Award`, `05_RankUp_Quiz_Business_QA` Auto-scoring and partial Marks):

```
CorrectPercentage = Floor((CorrectComponents / TotalComponents) × 100)
CalculatedMarks   = MaximumMarks × (CorrectComponents / TotalComponents)
AwardedMarks      = Floor(CalculatedMarks)
```

Always floor/truncate. Never `Math.Round`. 1.5→1, 1.9→1, 2.0→2.

| Type | Total components | Correct components |
|---|---|---|
| Multiple Choice | Expected correct options (not all options) | How many of those the student selected |
| Matching | Required pairs | Pairs matched correctly (index-aligned) |
| Ordering | Items that must be placed | Items in the correct position |

## Slot alignment (Match / Order)

`selectedOptionIds` is right-ids (Match) or option-ids (Order) **in slot order**. Unmatched/empty slots stay `0` (persisted as `null`). Do **not** drop zeros or `Distinct()` these lists — that shifts later pairs onto earlier slots.

Multiple Choice uses set semantics (`Distinct`, `id > 0`). Extra wrong MC selections are not extra components.

## Out of scope

Single Choice, True/False, Media: all-or-nothing. Fill in the Blanks: full accepted-answer match only. Essay / File Upload: never auto-marked.
